Z||000000||e007dw||03-22-2001||10:28 AM||||My 85 4cyl has a noisy alternator belt and I'd like to change it.<P>Any tips?<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||03-22-2001||04:04 PM||||<BR>Wow! Can't believe no one has replied to your query. Anyway. Welcome to the Forum.<P>A thought regarding the belt.  How old is the belt?  If it is fairly new, did you restretch the alternator to make the belt tighter?<P>This somewhat simple question has plagued many a fiero owner, just check the search function - it should turn up a whole heck of alot of stuff.<P>Anyway, if the belt is old, put on a new one.  And I seem to remember reading somewhere on the forum, something about the number of teeth on the v-belt, so try looking that up.<P>Others have tried belt dressing, and other things, and have not had success.<P>It may be possible that the alternator, the water pump and crank are not operating on the same plain. Maybe the alternator bracket is slightly bent which is causing the belt to rub.<P>Just my few thoughts. Again, welcome to the Forum and good luck.<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Not So Fair Weather Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||03-22-2001||06:23 PM||||Not all belts are created equal, I purchased a belt from Discount auto for $7 and it would squeal all the time. I lost the belt one day and had to buy one from Firestone $14 no more squeaks. The one from discount was around 3/8 think and the one from Firestone was a good ½ thick. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
